{
  "_comment": "Vorlage fuer ~/.claude/settings.json. NICHT einfach drueberkopieren — der Installer MERGED sie in eine vorhandene settings.json (Backup vorher, Hook-Arrays additiv mit Duplikat-Check ueber den command-String). Platzhalter: <<NODE>> = Pfad zur node-Executable (oder schlicht 'node', wenn es auf dem PATH liegt), <<CLAUDE_DIR>> = dein Claude-Ordner (i.d.R. ~/.claude), <<VAULT_ROOT>> = dein Obsidian-Vault. Alle drei muessen ersetzt sein, sonst feuern die Hooks ins Leere.",
  "env": {
    "AGENTICOS_VAULT": "<<VAULT_ROOT>>"
  },
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "<<NODE>> \"<<CLAUDE_DIR>>/hooks/context-mode-cache-heal.mjs\""
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "<<NODE>> \"<<CLAUDE_DIR>>/skills/task-roadmap/aggregate.js\"",
            "timeout": 10,
            "async": true
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "<<NODE>> \"<<CLAUDE_DIR>>/hooks/skill-gate.js\"",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "<<NODE>> \"<<CLAUDE_DIR>>/hooks/tooling-discipline-guard.js\"",
            "timeout": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "<<NODE>> \"<<CLAUDE_DIR>>/hooks/plan-first-guard.js\"",
            "timeout": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "<<NODE>> \"<<CLAUDE_DIR>>/hooks/ui-skill-hint.js\"",
            "timeout": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "<<NODE>> \"<<CLAUDE_DIR>>/hooks/large-change-hint.js\"",
            "timeout": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "<<NODE>> \"<<CLAUDE_DIR>>/hooks/db-skill-hint.js\"",
            "timeout": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "<<NODE>> \"<<CLAUDE_DIR>>/hooks/memory-tags-guard.js\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "<<NODE>> \"<<CLAUDE_DIR>>/hooks/vault-wikilink.js\"",
            "timeout": 10,
            "async": true
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "<<NODE>> \"<<CLAUDE_DIR>>/hooks/vault-read-order-hint.js\"",
            "timeout": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "<<NODE>> \"<<CLAUDE_DIR>>/hooks/skill-routing-reminder.js\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "<<NODE>> \"<<CLAUDE_DIR>>/hooks/review-gate.js\"",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "statusLine": {
    "type": "command",
    "command": "<<NODE>> \"<<CLAUDE_DIR>>/statusline/statusline.js\""
  },
  "autoMemoryEnabled": true,
  "autoMemoryDirectory": "<<VAULT_ROOT>>/memory",
  "skillListingBudgetFraction": 0.05,
  "alwaysThinkingEnabled": false,
  "tui": "fullscreen",
  "_hinweise": [
    "context-mode-cache-heal.mjs (SessionStart) nur bei installiertem context-mode-Plugin eintragen.",
    "aggregate.js (SessionStart) nur bei installiertem task-roadmap-Skill eintragen.",
    "Ohne gesetztes env.AGENTICOS_VAULT sind memory-tags-guard und vault-wikilink absichtlich inert.",
    "skill-gate.js (PreToolUse, deny) und review-gate.js (Stop, block) sind SCHARFE Gates, kein Hinweistext: skill-gate blockt groessere Code-Writes ohne vorherigen Superpowers-Process-Skill, review-gate blockt das Turn-Ende nach security-relevantem Code ohne security-reviewer-Lauf. Beide throtteln auf 1x pro Session (skill-gate: pro Datei) — der zweite Versuch laeuft bewusst durch (Escape-Hatch, kein Defekt). Wer die Gates nicht will, entfernt die beiden Eintraege."
  ]
}
